Split ESP32-S3 IRAM around the DCache hole to fix SIMPLE_BOOT boot hang

boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld

WHY
---
The SIMPLE_BOOT image dies inside bootloader_init() (TG0WDT reset loop).
Root cause: the ESP32-S3 DCache physically owns SRAM 0x40378000-0x4037C000
(16 KB).  The ROM bootloader copies the IRAM segment from flash to IRAM
through the 0x3C800000 cache window; writes that land in that 16 KB hole are
silently swallowed by the cache controller, so bootloader_init() code is read
back as all-zeros and the CPU IllegalInstruction-faults.  Forensics (run88 MAP
probe) pinned the zero region exactly to dst [0x40378000,0x4037C000).

FIX
---
iram0_0_seg currently spans 0x40374000 -> SRAM_IRAM_END and straddles the hole.
Split it into two hole-free regions:/n  iram0_0_seg : org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG (0x40374000), len = 0x4000  (vectors only)
  iram0_1_seg : org = 0x4037C000,          len = SRAM_IRAM_END - 0x4037C000
and route .iram0.text / .iram0.text_end / .iram0.data / .iram0.bss to
iram0_1_seg.  .iram0.vectors stays in iram0_0_seg (region A) so vecbase and
the reset vector table are untouched.  No loaded IRAM lands in the hole, so
the ROM copy is no longer corrupted.

This is the real fix for the boot hang; the debug probes 0003/0004 can be
reverted once a clean boot is confirmed.

diff --git a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
index 305256c..13bd98b 100644
--- a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
+++ b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@ SECTIONS
     . = ALIGN(4) + 16;
 
     _iram_text = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
     /* Marks the end of IRAM code segment */
 
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ SECTIONS
     . += 16;
     . = ALIGN(256);
     _iram_end = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .iram0.data :
   {
@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@ SECTIONS
 
     *(.iram.data)
     *(.iram.data.*)
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .iram0.bss (NOLOAD) :
   {
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@ SECTIONS
 
     . = ALIGN(4);
     _iram_end = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .dram0.dummy (NOLOAD) :
   {
diff --git a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
index ee0e928..0e6e869 100644
--- a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
+++ b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
@@ -118,7 +118,14 @@ MEMORY
 
   /* IRAM for CPU */
 
-  iram0_0_seg (RX) :                 org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG, len = SRAM_IRAM_SIZE
+  /* IRAM split around the ESP32-S3 DCache hole at 0x40378000-0x4037C000.
+   * The cache controller owns that 16 KB; when the ROM bootloader copies the
+   * IRAM segment through the 0x3C800000 cache window, writes landing there are
+   * silently dropped, corrupting bootloader_init() and causing the TG0WDT reset
+   * loop (SIMPLE_BOOT).  Route loaded IRAM to two hole-free regions instead.
+   */
+  iram0_0_seg (RX) :                 org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG, len = 0x4000
+  iram0_1_seg (RX) :                 org = 0x4037C000, len = SRAM_IRAM_END - 0x4037C000
 
   /* Flash mapped instruction data. */
 
